==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Dark PPT48''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''PPT46''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
PPT48's stats are highly unbalanced against her; with virtually no health and damage, she has no real impact in fights, exception made for the very beginning of the game. Her only real redeeming quality is the ability, which, however, has both low cooldown and uptime, as well as low compatibility on Darks, high competition and a tendency to never be applied due to how easily this unit dies.

Her use is not recommended, but, if used, she should at the very least be limited to Dark-heavy stages only, where she should be used in tandem with other stallers while being heavily defended.

==='''True Form'''===
PPT46 and her squad of cats are still pretty weak, but the acceptable recharge for her kind of unit and increased attack rate make her much better.

Despite everything, she is still rarely worth using outside stages that feature many Dark enemies, as her stats, even when boosted, lead to a unit who is highly unfit for generalist work.

Against Dark enemies, she has the advantage that it may be possible to stack some of her to get a consistent effect on those with medium range, problem is... there aren't really any and there are plenty of better options for shorter-ranged foes.

=== '''Talents''' ===
'''Recover Speed Up''' is a solid talent. It gives the unit more spammability, which is important for a 40% freeze proc unit, though it is a tad expensive for only about a little over 3 seconds off the top. Not a bad investment if you use PPT46 unit a lot and/or have NP to spare.

'''Attack Buff''' and '''HP Buff''' are fairly useless, as PPT46 is a CC unit with bad stats despite her low recharge time and cost.

'''Curse Immunity''' is completely useless. PPT46 has no anti-relic capabilities, and even if she did, or on stages with Dark, Angel and Relic enemies, anything that does curse her will very likely also kill her. DO NOT PURCHASE THIS.

'''Target Angel''' is easily her best and most interesting talent. Unlike Dark enemies, the Angel freeze niche is much less filled, especially for spammable units. And when it comes to spammable units, PPT46 has most of them beat. Her range is what gives her the upper hand against a wide variety of potent angel threats. Unlike [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet Cat]], her main competition, she outranges [[Angelic Sleipnir]], [[Winged Pigge]], [[Heavenly Le'saint]] and many others. This talent allows her to become a very strong unit in this niche and therefore making this a very worthwhile talent.

